; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Procedure Toolbox
; CATEGORY: Files & Data
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     savel, load, define, text, erase, workspace
; SUMMARY:  Builds new drawing procedures with DEFINE, saves them to a toolbox file with SAVEL, forgets them and loads them back.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Procedures are data too. This program writes three new procedures
;   while it runs, using DEFINE with a list of lines: TRIANGLE, PENTAGON
;   and HEXAGON, all made by one maker procedure. It saves them into
;   /projects/toolbox.lgo with SAVEL, erases them (so Logo no longer
;   knows them), then LOADs the file and uses the tools to draw a
;   pattern. Any later program can LOAD the same toolbox.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Open /projects/toolbox.lgo afterwards: it is ordinary
;   Logo with TO and END, written by the program. In the command
;   center try  LOAD "/projects/toolbox.lgo  and then  HEXAGON 50
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * DEFINE "name [[inputs] [line 1] [line 2]] makes a procedure
;   * TEXT outputs a procedure as that same list
;   * SAVEL, ERASE, PROCEDUREP and LOAD
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Add OCTAGON to the toolbox
;   * Make a maker for stars instead of polygons
;   * Save the toolbox, then LOAD it in a new program of your own
; ============================================================

make "toolbox "/projects/toolbox.lgo

; Build a polygon procedure called NAME with SIDES sides.
; The procedure it makes takes one input, the length of a side.
to make.polygon.tool :name :sides
  define :name (list [size] (list "repeat :sides (list "fd ":size "rt 360 / :sides)))
end

to tool.names
  output [triangle pentagon hexagon]
end

make.polygon.tool "triangle 3
make.polygon.tool "pentagon 5
make.polygon.tool "hexagon 6
print [DEFINE made this procedure from a list:]
show text "hexagon

savel tool.names :toolbox
print (sentence [Saved] tool.names [to] :toolbox)

foreach tool.names [erase ?]
print (sentence [After ERASE, is HEXAGON a procedure?] procedurep "hexagon)

load :toolbox
print (sentence [After LOAD, is HEXAGON a procedure?] procedurep "hexagon)

; Now use the reloaded tools: three rings, one per tool.
clearscreen hideturtle setpensize 2
make "colors [4 2 1]
foreach tool.names [
  localmake "tool ?
  setpencolor item # :colors
  repeat 12 [
    penup home setheading repcount * 30 fd 40 * # pendown
    run (list :tool 30)
  ]
]
